WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:06.120
Every new month brings a guarantee of fresh,
original Netflix programming, but March 2019

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.180
is going to be the motherload.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.860
With a grand total of 60 Netflix originals
heading onto the streaming service, you're

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.560
all but guaranteed to find something new to
fall in love with.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.660
No matter how you break it down, there's going
to be a ton of streaming options crashing

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.800
onto Netflix over the next 31 days.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.970
So we picked through the mass of new releases
to come up with the best, most exciting, and

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.940
most original Netflix releases for March 2019.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.740
History generally focuses on the winners.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.680
But what about those men and women who poured
their hearts and souls into something, only

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.760
to come up short?

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.760
What about the losers of history?

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.800
"You are one pathetic loser.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:43.640
No offense."

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.500
But what if it's our losses that give us strength
to keep fighting?

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.100
That's what Netflix's upcoming documentary
Losers wants to know.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.860
By looking at the people who didn't bring
home the top prize, Losers explores what lessons

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.340
we can all learn from...well, losing.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.080
Take a look on March 1st.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.420
Directed by and starring Chiwetel Ejiofor,
The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind tells the dramatic

00:01:05.429 --> 00:01:10.590
story of a 14-year-old boy in Malawi who builds
a windmill generator to help his famine-stricken

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.080
village.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.640
The film dropped at Sundance in January 2019
to extremely positive reviews and snagged

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.480
the Alfred P. Sloan Feature Film Prize in
the process.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:24.000
If the premise sounds familiar, that's because
it's based on the real-life story of William

00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:28.099
Kamkwamba, who went on to give a TED talk
about his experiences bringing electricity

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.640
and irrigation to his village.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.820
Get ready for a powerful hit of emotion when
The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind blows onto

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.240
Netflix on March 1st.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.799
The political thriller Secret City largely
flew under the radar when it premiered on

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.980
Netflix in June 2018, but the critical reception
was overwhelmingly positive.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.900
Dark and cerebral, Secret City follows a journalist,
played by Anna Torv, who digs too deep while

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.800
investigating a government conspiracy.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.160
The second season promises more of the same
suspense and political intrigue as the first

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:57.660
season.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.560
Take a look on March 6th.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:04.680
On the heels of hit supernatural shows like
Sabrina and Umbrella Academy, Netflix is dropping

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:06.639
the first season of The Order.

00:02:06.639 --> 00:02:10.910
The show centers on a college freshman who
joins a secret society and gets caught up

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.250
in a battle against evil werewolves.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:14.250
Like you do.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:18.269
The trailer for The Order promises a little
magic, a little mayhem, and a lot of drama

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:21.069
perfect for bingeing through those cold March
nights.

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:22.260
Check it out on March 7.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:27.159
Anyone familiar with Ricky Gervais' style
of comedy should have some idea of what to

00:02:27.159 --> 00:02:28.870
expect in After Life.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.569
In the show, Gervais plays a writer whose
wife passes away, leading him to adopt a bitter

00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:34.599
outlook on the world.

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:36.830
"If you're watching this then I’m not around
anymore.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.170
But don’t spiral, don’t obsess.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.219
Keep going."

00:02:40.219 --> 00:02:44.219
Although details about the show have been
few and far between, Gervais explained a bit

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.500
about his character's headspace to SiriusXM's
Ron Bennington.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.180
"So it's a good guy trying to be a psychopath,
because he's hurt."

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:52.220
Dark?

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.480
Yeah, pretty much.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.320
Funny?

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.080
We hope so!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.560
Tune in when After Life drops on March 8.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.840
In Formula 1: Drive to Survive, Netflix is
looking behind the scenes of the ultra-competitive

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.480
world of Formula 1 racing.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:09.739
This high-octane documentary series puts viewers
in the driver's seat to experience the thrill

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:14.230
of victory, the despair of defeat, and the
white-knuckle adrenaline of one of the fastest

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.049
sports on four wheels.

00:03:16.049 --> 00:03:20.190
Anchoring it all are the stories of the dedicated
drivers who put their lives on the line for

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.860
glory, fame, and fortune.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.580
Formula 1: Drive to Survive races onto Netflix
on March 8.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:30.620
According to the Netflix series page, Immortals
is about a vampire who's out for vengeance

00:03:30.629 --> 00:03:35.920
against the leader of her own kind, a ruthless
killer who's attempting to gain immortality.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.750
And sure, another modern-day vampire yarn
doesn't exactly bleed originality, but we're

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.030
hoping this turns out to be worth watching.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.200
Find out on March 8th.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.200
Shadow

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.079
South African cinema hasn't had a whole lot
of representation on Netflix, but that's set

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.060
to change with the addition of the Netflix
original Shadow.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.360
Part cop drama and part vigilante justice,
Shadow focuses on a former policeman who was

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.920
struck by lightning and loses the ability
to feel pain.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.980
What else would you do with a power like that
besides go after the city's bad guys one by

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:05.480
one?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.760
But if Dexter taught us anything all those
years ago, it's that the real police force

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.920
doesn't always like having a rogue criminal
catcher on the loose.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.320
"He's playing god, and sooner or later he's
going to fall from his tower."

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:21.880
Will he be able to make a dent in crime when
he's being pursued by both sides of the law?

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.660
Find out when the action-packed new series
premieres on March 8th.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:29.660
Ben Affleck headlines Triple Frontier as a
retired soldier who gets pulled into a criminal

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:33.480
heist when one of his war buddies decides
to get their old crew together.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.170
His plan is to take out a drug cartel boss
and rob his house.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:41.130
Of course, that's the kind of plan that's
bound to go disastrously wrong, and you can

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.780
probably expect plenty of twists as the story
unfolds.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.580
"A lot more people are going to come after
you.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.820
You lied to us."

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:53.040
Oscar Isaac and Charlie Hunnam costar in Triple
Frontier, which hits Netflix on March 13.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:57.660
Arrested Development has come a long way from
its beginnings as a troubled Fox series to

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.720
its current status as a Netflix original.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:04.740
As the third season of the original series
faced cancellation due to a dwindling audience,

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:08.379
the showrunners even worked a few cries for
help into the story itself.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.520
"Instead of us all selling out and becoming
housewives and waiters, why don’t we have

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.440
a big event?

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.180
Some sort of Save Our Bluth’s type thing?"

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.759
Fortunately, Netflix finally picked up the
show in 2006, streaming all three original

00:05:22.759 --> 00:05:25.610
seasons while filming a fourth and fifth season.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.759
On March 15th, you can check out the final
half of Season 5.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.860
If you miss it, there'll only be one thing
you can say:

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:35.020
"I've made a huge mistake."

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:39.040
Burn Out follows a professional motorcycle
rider who's one of the best racers on the

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:39.540
track.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.400
But when his mom's life is threatened by the
criminal underworld, he'll have to use his

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:48.160
need for speed to ferry drugs, all in the
hopes of paying off his mother's debt.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.400
Filled with suspense and motorcycle chases,
Burn Out looks like a great film for any action

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.449
lovers out there.

00:05:53.449 --> 00:05:55.440
Saddle up when Burn Out arrives on March 15th.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.040
What is Love, Death &amp; Robots?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.940
According to Netflix's official description,
it's an animated anthology involving, quote

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:07.069
"terrifying creatures, wicked surprises, and
dark comedy."

00:06:07.069 --> 00:06:11.550
That sounds interesting, and even more intriguing
is the fact that Love, Death &amp; Robots comes

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.480
from David Fincher and Deadpool director Tim
Miller.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.540
Animation or not, you'll definitely want to
put the tots to bed before queuing up any

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:19.819
of these mature shorts.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.540
For his part, Tim Miller has called the project
a labor of love, saying that he's...

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:28.229
"[...] excited that the creative landscape
has finally changed enough for adult-themed

00:06:28.229 --> 00:06:31.669
animation to become part of a larger cultural
conversation."

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:35.660
Take a look when all 18 episodes of Love,
Death &amp; Robots drop on March 15th.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.580
The initial news of a revival of the mid-aughts
makeover show Queer Eye for the Straight Guy

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:45.530
was met with mixed responses, but in the true
spirit of the show, the modern makeover turned

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.280
out to have just the right stuff for today's
world.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:52.960
With a new "Fab Five" with expertise in design,
culture, and fashion, Queer Eye showed that

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:57.400
it was willing to delve deeper than a superficial
makeover, tackling issues like homophobia,

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.260
racism, and police profiling.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:01.820
"I love the fab five.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.700
They made me feel great."

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.930
Season 2 was met with the same positive response,
and now fans are gearing up for a third season,

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:10.300
which drops on March 15th.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:15.220
Mötley Crüe has spent almost four decades
shaking stadiums with their mix of heavy metal

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:16.200
and glam rock.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.270
But even more than their music, the band was
all-too-often known for their hard-rocking

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.819
lifestyles filled with drugs and parties.

00:07:22.819 --> 00:07:27.599
Based on the band's own autobiography, The
Dirt offers a cinematic look behind Mötley

00:07:27.599 --> 00:07:28.620
Crüe's music.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:32.560
It's sure to be a pulse-pounding biopic, and
you can take the ride on March 22nd.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:38.260
The suburban zombie comedy Santa Clarita Diet
shouldn't work as well as it does, but fans

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:42.910
have spent two seasons growing to love the
characters of this quirky, funny, and occasionally

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.080
graphically violent show.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.220
"That was a crazy amount of vomit"

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.460
“Well, I’m not a medical expert so I can’t
say what the proper amount of vomit is.”

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.760
"It was a HUGE amount."

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:56.990
For those who haven't caught the bug yet,
Santa Clarita Diet stars Drew Barrymore as

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.550
a real estate agent who's unfortunately turned
into a zombie.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:05.360
It's up to her husband, played by Josh Duhamel,
to help her satisfy her hunger for human flesh

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.830
while also making sure they all keep up the
standards of their upper middle class lifestyle.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.520
"Excuse me, I gotta go lie to a cop and tell
him I murdered someone so I don't get in trouble."

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:18.080
Tune in for Season 3 on March 29th.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:23.479
The story of Bonnie and Clyde is the stuff
of legends...and like most legends, it's been

00:08:23.479 --> 00:08:26.180
adapted for film and television way too many
times.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:30.939
The outlaw lovers even got the campy revised
history treatment with Bonnie &amp; Clyde vs.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:31.440
Dracula.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:35.940
When your true story of love and murder needs
vampires to liven it up, you know it's been

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:36.820
done to death.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.400
So what makes The Highwaymen different?

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:44.060
For starters, it shifts the focus from Clyde
Barrow and Bonnie Parker onto Frank Hamer

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.820
and Maney Gault, two aging Texas rangers who
joined the hunt for Bonnie and Clyde and were

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:51.100
eventually responsible for bringing them down.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.720
Woody Harrelson and Kevin Costner take the
lead roles, promising a gritty, emotional

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:56.560
detective drama.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.700
Take a look when The Highwaymen lands on March
29.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.711
New original comedy

00:09:00.711 --> 00:09:04.650
Comedy fans will have plenty to look forward
to this March, with four new stand-up specials

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.280
joining the streaming service.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.540
For starters, look for the political comedy
show Patriot Act with Hasan Minhaj, airing

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.240
every week starting March 3.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:17.000
On the 12th, tune in for British comedian
Jimmy Carr's The Best of Ultimate Gold Greatest

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:17.500
Hits.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:22.620
After that, Amy Schumer's bringing her newest
special, Growing, on March 12, and Nate Bargatze

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:26.370
drops an hour of standup on the 26th with
The Tennessee Kid.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.060
Those are all the best Netflix originals to
look forward to.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.920
Now here are some new movies hitting the service
in March.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:37.700
Two kung fu masterpieces and an off-the-wall
family adventure mark Netflix's action additions

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:38.700
this March.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:42.780
On the first of the month, Crouching Tiger,
Hidden Dragon sails onto the service.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:47.530
On the 8th, gather up the family and queue
up Spy Kids 2: The Island of Lost Dreams,

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:50.840
easily one of the most bizarre family films
in recent history.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:54.100
"Smells like the work of Donovan Giggles."

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:59.700
And on the 15th, don't miss Stephen Chow's
hilarious action comedy Kung Fu Hustle.

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:04.890
Speaking of comedy, March is all about the
classics, with 2001's ridiculous farce Wet

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:09.640
Hot American Summer showing up on the first,
followed by the horror comedy Tucker and Dale

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:11.220
vs. Evil on the 29th.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.100
"He gonna walk it off.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:13.960
He's gonna be fine."

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.120
There'll also be some more serious fare arriving
in March.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:21.450
On the first, relive the indy thriller that
put Jennifer Lawrence on the map Winter's

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:21.940
Bone.

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:27.020
This haunting mystery revolves around a young
girl on the hunt for her father in the Ozarks

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:30.560
and features a powerhouse performance from
Lawrence as the lead character.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.140
There will be plenty of new drama additions
as well.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.520
On the first of the month, keep your eyes
peeled for Stanley Kubrick's A Clockwork Orange,

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:40.380
Apollo 13, and The Hurt Locker, among others.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.740
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:45.880
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.700
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

